## THE CROSSING AND THE WOODS WITH PIETER (`story.ni:6829`, `6880-6958`).
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## `story.ni:6829`, once — before going north from the Crossing with Pieter;
## spoken on the Woods' arrival as Chapter 4 spoke the wobble.

define phrase skirts-over-the-stream
  Now that you've had a bit of practice, you're a bit more confident on the
  rocks this time. Carefully lifting your skirts (you're still getting used
  to moving around in a dress), you pick your way over the stream with
  little difficulty.

  Pieter, on the other hand, stumbles halfway across and lurches into the
  water, soaking his trousers up to the knee. You do your best to stifle
  your laughter as he sloshes his way to shore, cursing and grumbling
  something about 'gratitude' and 'youth today.'
end phrase

## `story.ni:6885`

define phrase where-was-the-sapling
  The game trails criss-cross through the woods in every direction, and they
  all look the same. When you were here the night before, Bobby quickly
  found a shortcut to the clearing. Where was it?
end phrase

## `story.ni:6929`, by the sapling's way.

define phrase sapling-found-north
  You search the underbrush carefully. At first it all looks the same, but
  after several tense minutes... you find it! The split sapling that Bobby
  showed you last night, right next to a trail leading north.
end phrase

