## THE CLEARING WITH PIETER (`story.ni:6978`, `7032-7035`).
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

define phrase cant-turn-back-now
  You can't turn back now — and besides, it would take you all night to find
  your way back out of those woods.
end phrase

define phrase bolt-opens-the-entrance
  The metal knob pushes in, then pops out again with a click. Suddenly there
  is a deep, solid thunk, and a scraping sound coming from the stone beneath
  you. Just as it did before, part of the statue's base swings inward.

  Pieter raises his eyebrows. 'Huh,' he says, 'I never knew about that.'
end phrase

