## THE WALL, THE HOLE, THE BRICK AND THE LEVER (`story.ni:7216-7307`) — the
## way in alone. The hole is offstage until her fingers find it; the brick
## rests in it; the lever is offstage until the brick comes out.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## `story.ni:7250`

define phrase fingertips-find-the-hole
  Carefully, you run your fingertips across the wall, trying to remember
  where Bobby found the loose brick the last time you were here.

  Ah-ha! You find it — the faint outline of a rectangular hole, with a brick
  resting loosely in the gap.
end phrase

## `story.ni:7235`, the sealed wall once the hole is found.

define phrase wall-with-the-hole
  It's just a blank, featureless, stone wall... except for the rough,
  rectangular hole where one of the bricks is missing.
end phrase

## `story.ni:7256`

define phrase wall-no-obvious-means
  The wall has no obvious means of opening. You seem to remember Bobby doing
  something with a loose brick...
end phrase

## `story.ni:7245`

define phrase leave-the-wall-open
  Better leave it open. You might need a quick getaway later on, and you
  can't be sure that the wall won't lock behind you if you close it.
end phrase

create the rectangular hole
  aka hole, rough hole, rectangle, gap, rough rectangular hole
  a container
  scenery

  In the back of the hole you see a short lever.

  on the player examining
    phrase brick-is-loose-here when the brick is in the rectangular hole
    phrase lever-in-the-hole when the brick is not in the rectangular hole
  end on

  on the player searching
    phrase brick-is-loose-here when the brick is in the rectangular hole
    phrase lever-in-the-hole when the brick is not in the rectangular hole
  end on

  on the player inserting
    refuse when the brick is in the rectangular hole: cant-fit-in-the-hole
  end on

  after the player inserting
    phrase brick-slides-back when the brick is in the rectangular hole
    move the short lever offstage when the brick is in the rectangular hole
  end after

## `story.ni:7266` — the hole's look and search: the brick while it is
## there, the lever once it is out. The container report lists the brick
## by itself; the lever's sentence is the description.

define phrase cant-fit-in-the-hole
  You can't quite fit that into the hole; it keeps bumping into something
  back in there.
end phrase

define phrase brick-slides-back
  The brick slides easily back into the hole.
end phrase

define phrase brick-is-loose-here
  The brick is loose here.
end phrase

define phrase lever-in-the-hole
  In the back of the hole you see a short lever.
end phrase

## `pull brick` is taking it (`story.ni:7278`): the brick is pullable so
## the pull reaches its clause, which does the take's work.

create the brick
  aka loose brick, stone
  pullable
  in the rectangular hole

  You see nothing special about the brick.

  phrase detail while the brick is in the rectangular hole:
    The brick is loose here.

  on the player pulling
    phrase brick-pulled-out when the brick is in the rectangular hole
    move the short lever to the Tunnel End when the brick is in the rectangular hole
    move the brick to the player when the brick is in the rectangular hole
  end on

  on the player pushing
    refuse when the brick is in the rectangular hole: brick-does-not-push
  end on

  on the player turning
    refuse when the brick is in the rectangular hole: brick-does-not-turn
  end on

  after the player taking
    phrase brick-pulled-out when the short lever is not in the Tunnel End
    move the short lever to the Tunnel End
  end after

define phrase brick-does-not-push
  The brick does not push in. You might be able to pull it out, though.
end phrase

define phrase brick-does-not-turn
  The brick does not turn. You might be able to pull it out, though.
end phrase

