## `story.ni:7307`

define phrase lever-opens-the-wall
  The lever moves slightly, then snaps back with a click. The wall swings
  away, revealing shadows beyond.

  Pieter looks impressed. 'You're full of secrets and surprises, aren't
  you?' You can't bring yourself to tell him that you learned all your
  secrets from Bobby.
end phrase

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## THE LOWER BAILEY ON BALL NIGHT (`story.ni:7372`, `7424-7428`).
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

define phrase bailey-for-the-ball, stopping while bodyguarded
  The lower bailey has been cleaned, with gravel spread over the larger mud
  puddles. Guests to the ball are still trickling in from the south. The
  doors to the inner keep stand open to the north, and music and laughter
  drift out into the evening air.
end phrase

define phrase bailey-in-shadow, stopping while not bodyguarded
  A thick wedge of shadow falls across the courtyard at the base of the
  Keep's outer wall, providing a relatively safe place to hide. The rest of
  the courtyard is flooded with moonlight, and bored-looking guards stroll
  back and forth over the gravel. You can return to the Chapel to the
  northeast.
end phrase

define phrase bailey-up-attention
  Climbing up to the upper bailey would only attract unwanted attention. The
  ball is where you need to be.
end phrase

