## THE FOYER (`story.ni:11021-11046`) — the source's Entrance Hall, printed
## "Foyer"; Red Gate Estate holds the source's name, so this is the Foyer.
## Chapter 11's ballroom lies north as a placeholder.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

create the Foyer
  a room
  aka entrance hall, hall, inner keep, castle, keep
  north to the Ballroom
  south is blocked while the preparations is journey: dont-lose-your-nerve

  The entrance hall has been decorated for the occasion, its stark, stone
  walls hidden behind festive tapestries and garlands. A few guests stand
  around in groups, chatting, but the main event seems to be in the
  ballroom, north of here. {pieter-bodyguard}

  after the player entering
    first time
      phrase foyer-arrival
  end after

## `story.ni:11040-11043`, once — the port's Chapter 10 ends here; the
## source's "Chapter 10 - The Ball" heading is the port's Chapter XI row,
## one step north.

define phrase foyer-arrival
  A servant in formal livery bows, then takes your and Pieter's cloaks and
  deftly spirits them away.

  Pieter takes a deep breath. 'Well, we made it,' he whispers. 'Although
  frankly, I'd rather we were still sneaking through dark, dirty tunnels. I
  guess you'd better head into the ballroom and start mingling.'
end phrase

define phrase dont-lose-your-nerve
  Pieter puts his hand on your back, gently but firmly. 'Don't lose your
  nerve now,' he says. 'You'll be fine; I'll be right behind you the whole
  time.'
end phrase

define phrase foyer-music-and-laughter
  You can hear the sounds of laughter and music coming from the ballroom to
  the north.
end phrase

create the tapestries
  aka tapestry, hangings, hanging, battle, battles, battle scenes, scenes, scene, noblemen, nobleman, nobles, soldiers, soldier, coats of arms, coat of arms, western clans, clans, clan, war
  scenery, plural
  in the Foyer

  The tapestries depict important battles in the history of Miradania,
  noblemen leading their soldiers into war against the western clans. You
  see a number of coats-of-arms represented in the battle scenes.
  Interestingly, Fossville's is not among them.

create the garlands
  aka garland, greenery, festive greenery
  scenery, plural
  in the Foyer

  The garlands add a touch of festive greenery to the room.

## THE BALLROOM is Chapter 11's (`ball.chord`); the Foyer's north reaches
## it by name.
